The voice screen is no longer somewhere the app can be parked. Leave and come back and you are on the door, which is where the app is useful.

Every tap now tells you it landed. Opening the mic and closing it before speaking were both completely silent before, so a command it failed to catch gave you nothing at all. The buzzes are a language now: opening, understood, halfway, sent, stopped, and did-not-take each feel different, so your wrist alone tells you what happened.
